      "Saint John Paul II": 1,
      "Karol Wojtyła, born in 1920 in Wadowice, Poland, lost his mother at nine and his brother at twelve. During the German occupation he worked in a stone quarry and a chemical plant, then was ordained a priest in 1946. Elected pope in 1978, he cried out at his inaugural Mass on October 22: “Do not be afraid! Open wide the doors to Christ!” He died on April 2, 2005, was beatified in 2011 and declared a saint in 2014.": 1,
      "Brief story based on Vatican News' saint of the day.": 1,
