      "Saint Arethas and Companions": 1,
      "Arethas was an elderly Christian leader in Najran, a town in South Arabia and a center of Christianity there. Around 523, a local ruler besieged Najran and promised amnesty if the town surrendered. Arethas warned the people, but they surrendered. Arethas and many others, including priests, deacons, monks and consecrated virgins, were put to death because they would not deny that Christ is God. The Church remembers Arethas and his companions as martyrs on October 24.": 1,
      "Brief story based on the New Catholic Encyclopedia, via Encyclopedia.com.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Arethas and his companions": 1,
